  "solution": {
    "text": "When viewed from spherical side,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>32</mn></mfrac></math><br />Image position is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;inside the hemisphere from its periphery.<br />And when viewed from plane side then image is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;inside the plane surface.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>&#916;x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>"
